1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,240
I've been going to WWDC since 2011.

2
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:05,360
The last time Steve Jobs spoke there,

3
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:07,260
and every year I try to guess,

4
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:10,680
is Apple going to come out with something completely new

5
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:12,900
or they only get about to make last year's thing

6
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:14,160
10% better.

7
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:17,520
When Apple first introduced ARKit, I was really excited.

8
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:20,040
But after a few versions, I started wondering,

9
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:22,320
what are they actually building toward?

10
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:26,160
Apple doesn't hire a bunch of computer PhDs

11
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:28,360
to develop some sort of technology

12
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:30,360
just for somebody to hold an iPhone up

13
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:32,120
until their shoulder gives out.

14
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:34,880
There had to be another piece of hardware in the works.

15
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:38,800
WWDC, when Apple finally announced the Vision Pro,

16
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:41,360
they showed it to us and we could look at it,

17
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:45,080
but we couldn't touch it, which was exquisite torture.

18
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:48,560
Once preo orders opened, I was on my iPhone immediately.

19
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:50,080
And on launch day, I picked up one

20
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:52,120
of the first Vision Pros in Dallas.

